{"check": "gp4_c2", "calls_counted": 4, "error": null, "wall_ms": 394, "cost_usd": 0.0018197340000000002, "items": [{"n": 1, "sentence": "The typical symptoms of GERD are heartburn and regurgitation of stomach contents into the throat", "approved": true}, {"n": 2, "sentence": "The condition happens when stomach contents flow back into the esophagus or mouth, and it can damage the esophagus over time", "approved": false}, {"n": 3, "sentence": "If left untreated, GERD can lead to serious problems including inflammation, narrowing of the esophagus, and a condition called Barrett esophagus, which can develop into esophageal cancer", "approved": false}, {"n": 4, "sentence": "In children, ordinary reflux is common and usually harmless, while GERD is a less common but more serious problem that may need treatment", "approved": false}, {"n": 5, "sentence": "In children, risk factors include abnormal relaxation of the valve between the stomach and esophagus, weakness in the esophageal lining, poor movement and emptying of the esophagus and stomach, and physical defects such as hiatal hernia", "approved": false}, {"n": 6, "sentence": "Reflux symptoms are among the most common reasons people visit their primary care doctor", "approved": false}, {"n": 7, "sentence": "Long-term use of the main medications used to treat GERD, called proton-pump inhibitors, can carry risks including bone fractures, kidney disease, pneumonia, and intestinal infection", "approved": false}, {"n": 8, "sentence": "In adults, reflux symptoms are typically evaluated with proton pump inhibitor trials, and certain situations call for referral to a gastroenterology specialist", "approved": false}], "phrases": {"pair_1_1": "of gastric", "pair_1_2": "gastric contents", "pair_1_3": "the oropharynx", "pair_2_1": "from the", "pair_2_2": "the reflux", "pair_2_3": "or oral", "pair_2_4": "symptoms or", "pair_2_5": "or complications", "pair_3_1": "gerd affects", "pair_3_2": "quality of", "pair_3_3": "of life", "pair_